Falsifies `address_space_map::verification::runtime_window_refuses_every_address_its_doc_forbids`.

The defect: `runtime_window` checks only the band's start, so an aligned address in the heap, the
image or anywhere above is returned as a runtime window.

Expected to fail: the harness reaches `refused_inputs_never_reach_here` (an unwinding failure, not a
panic), so Kani reports "encountered failures other than panics".

diff --git a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
index 0eba0def7..e1d60e4f6 100644
--- a/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/address_space_map/src/lib.rs
@@ -167,7 +167,7 @@ pub const fn runtime_window(va: u64) -> u64 {
         "a runtime window must be page aligned"
     );
     assert!(
-        RUNTIME_WINDOWS.contains(va),
+        va >= RUNTIME_WINDOWS.start,
         "a runtime window must lie in RUNTIME_WINDOWS (address_space_map)"
     );
     va
